{"id": "EUVD-2026-81984", "enisaUuid": "53ddf89e-c5b9-36c7-9875-d94685a112a1", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nublk: validate auto buf reg before taking uring_cmd\n\nWith UBLK_F_AUTO_BUF_REG, invalid sqe->addr can fail after\nublk_fill_io_cmd() has set UBLK_IO_FLAG_ACTIVE. The uring_cmd is\ncompleted while the tag stays active, which can hang teardown.\n\nSplit validation from buffer apply so the check has no side effects,\nthen take the uring_cmd and store the already-validated buffer. Apply\nthe same order in FETCH so io->buf is not written before __ublk_fetch()\nstate checks.", "datePublished": "2026-09-17T16:08:39", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-19T09:01:39", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/8397942b67128e0b1275cfedb5abf4faafac5fd0", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/653d22269a8b83b491f7f186a5d7872f14e6ddca", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/ca5a01eee34c7cbe0f531a613b0292a3ad1a419b"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-90323", "GHSA-rq26-mw8f-3hjh"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.21, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "48f57de3-ab4e-321c-9035-70b239b9c4e0", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.2.6"}, {"id": "68b48d69-84b6-3be3-a717-a68f1f915d07", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "52460dda3a775a73f226312b43c0a0211e8665ea <653d22269a8b83b491f7f186a5d7872f14e6ddca"}, {"id": "79b5f536-c1a6-3538-a8f3-ca59ebcc9583", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}, {"id": "907d2a2c-a985-3c23-9e67-34fc3c6bde1a", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "52460dda3a775a73f226312b43c0a0211e8665ea <ca5a01eee34c7cbe0f531a613b0292a3ad1a419b"}, {"id": "abb7aceb-5935-39fd-91a4-d34de01c02e5", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "6.17"}, {"id": "c730cd38-9fdb-3fab-8ed6-505669793147", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.18.57"}, {"id": "d86d45b5-4a9d-345f-9168-0e5290a028ff", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.3"}, {"id": "e0bc09ac-e25d-3600-ba99-7912c738cce1", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "52460dda3a775a73f226312b43c0a0211e8665ea <8397942b67128e0b1275cfedb5abf4faafac5fd0"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "f70542d2-3cc4-3197-8c29-54583d2d3437", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}], "isExploited": false}